WEBVTT

00:43.835 --> 00:48.339
DOONA!

01:43.978 --> 01:44.813
Doona.

01:45.563 --> 01:46.523
Lee Doona.

01:47.190 --> 01:48.233
Wake up.

01:49.442 --> 01:50.360
Lee Doona!

02:18.888 --> 02:23.768
EPISODE 2
GETTING TO KNOW EACH OTHER

02:30.942 --> 02:33.945
Jeong-hun consumes
150 grams of protein a day.

02:36.072 --> 02:38.908
His sole concern is
the peace and well-being of his body.

02:38.992 --> 02:42.495
Straighten your elbows out,
make them taut. That's it. Now breathe in.

02:42.579 --> 02:44.247
His dating views
are pretty rigid.

02:44.330 --> 02:46.249
Our population is out of control.

02:46.332 --> 02:48.168
It's not like propagation
is really needed.

02:48.251 --> 02:51.629
Our reproductive function in the future
should go through a degenerative process.

02:51.713 --> 02:54.174
That could be our next evolution.
Don't you think?

02:57.385 --> 02:58.511
Uh…

02:58.595 --> 03:00.930
Don't take any notice of him, babe.
He's an idiot.

03:01.014 --> 03:02.265
Say "ah."

03:02.348 --> 03:04.475
Yun-taek's nickname
is the Hundred-Day Prince.

03:04.559 --> 03:05.727
Right?

03:05.810 --> 03:07.228
He dreams of a fated love,

03:07.312 --> 03:10.607
but he can't ever go
more than 100 days without getting dumped.

03:11.816 --> 03:15.737
Of course, you won't always
know everyone's story entirely…

03:30.627 --> 03:33.004
…because we all have
a version of ourselves

03:34.297 --> 03:36.132
that we want to hide from the world.

03:38.801 --> 03:39.719
Hmm?

03:49.562 --> 03:52.774
CONVENIENCE STORE

03:55.818 --> 03:58.947
BLACK DEVIL GOLD

04:08.331 --> 04:09.290
Hey there.

04:09.374 --> 04:11.918
I sent a screenshot of the message
the boss sent me yesterday.

04:12.001 --> 04:13.127
That's it, right?

04:13.878 --> 04:16.005
Yeah, okay.

04:21.094 --> 04:22.011
Uh…

04:22.971 --> 04:23.805
Hey!

04:29.769 --> 04:30.603
Mmm.

04:40.363 --> 04:41.322
EDWARD

04:41.406 --> 04:44.284
So you'll go by Edward here.
We all go by English names.

04:44.367 --> 04:46.953
We really lucked out
you were available for hire so soon.

04:47.996 --> 04:49.163
Oh, look, there's Alice.

04:50.581 --> 04:51.749
No way!

04:52.583 --> 04:55.920
- Seriously, you're the new guy?
- Do you two know each other?

04:57.297 --> 04:58.881
Uh, yeah!

05:00.633 --> 05:01.676
What a coincidence.

05:02.677 --> 05:03.678
Welcome aboard.

05:08.224 --> 05:10.184
- Morning!
- Hello, welcome.

05:10.268 --> 05:12.562
- Can I have one iced Americano, please?
- Certainly.

05:12.645 --> 05:14.731
Mister, your iced hazelnut latte is ready.

05:15.231 --> 05:16.065
One moment.

05:16.149 --> 05:17.608
Enjoy your latte.

05:18.526 --> 05:19.819
Thank you so much.

05:32.999 --> 05:35.418
Oh!

05:48.890 --> 05:50.099
LEE DOONA
MISSED CALL

05:51.517 --> 05:52.518
Ah, that's cold!

05:54.228 --> 05:56.022
- Here you go.
- Oh, thanks so much.

06:01.402 --> 06:03.946
Ah, this is nice.

06:10.745 --> 06:12.163
You make good coffee.

06:12.246 --> 06:14.290
- It's good, right?
- Mm-hmm.

06:14.374 --> 06:15.333
Hmm.

06:16.334 --> 06:19.295
MARCH 2021 MOCK EXAM SCHOLARSHIP
1ST PLACE YANGJIN HIGH SCHOOL LEE WON-JUN

06:19.379 --> 06:21.464
2ND PLACE
YANGJIN GIRLS' HIGH SCHOOL KIM JIN-JU

06:27.095 --> 06:28.513
KIM JIN-JU
YANGJIN GIRLS' HIGH

06:35.353 --> 06:37.397
Oh? There's Kim Jin-ju.

06:37.480 --> 06:38.731
Do you know her?

06:38.815 --> 06:41.109
Uh, our restaurant's
in her family's building.

06:41.192 --> 06:43.194
They are super-duper rich.

06:43.694 --> 06:46.656
- Ah.
- Oh! Yu-i is there.

06:47.240 --> 06:49.158
Hey, I'll go say hi. I'll be back.

06:52.870 --> 06:54.330
Oh, got it!

06:55.998 --> 06:57.166
Okay, got it.

06:57.667 --> 06:59.419
Yeah!

07:07.176 --> 07:08.136
Excuse me.

07:08.219 --> 07:09.095
Hmm?

07:09.178 --> 07:11.180
- Oh!
- So I heard you're good with math.

07:11.264 --> 07:12.765
- Is that right?
- Mm-hmm.

07:12.849 --> 07:15.017
Do you think
you could help me with this?

07:20.690 --> 07:21.566
Mmm…

07:22.525 --> 07:23.693
Oh.

07:24.402 --> 07:25.361
- Oh.
- Here.

07:25.445 --> 07:26.279
Thank you.

07:27.822 --> 07:29.824
So, um, this triangle here…

07:33.578 --> 07:34.495
… cosine…

07:37.582 --> 07:38.791
Are you going home now?

07:39.292 --> 07:41.752
Uh, no. I'm heading to a tutoring gig.

07:41.836 --> 07:42.920
Oh.

07:43.963 --> 07:45.673
I work a lot, huh?

07:46.257 --> 07:48.384
You're not going through
any troubles now, are you?

07:49.010 --> 07:50.845
Why? You worried my family's going broke?

07:50.928 --> 07:52.430
No, no, no, that's not why.

07:53.431 --> 07:54.724
Well, I'm glad everything's good.

08:04.108 --> 08:04.942
Oh.

08:14.452 --> 08:17.371
ALICE

08:22.418 --> 08:23.794
Whenever I have tuna,

08:23.878 --> 08:27.215
I always kind of feel like
I've made it in life, you know?

08:27.298 --> 08:29.592
So I'm gonna lay down a bed of rice,

08:29.675 --> 08:33.596
and then I'll put this
in a fermented tuna chopsticks…

08:33.679 --> 08:34.847
Wait, what did I say?

08:35.431 --> 08:37.892
Now I have to warn you…

08:37.975 --> 08:40.645
So salty that you
really only have to add a tiny amount.

08:40.728 --> 08:41.771
MOM

08:41.854 --> 08:43.981
Next, you're gonna take some of this.

08:46.442 --> 08:49.487
Kind of like making sushi.
Well, that's what it feels like.

08:49.570 --> 08:52.114
Use a little
of the sesame-oil-and-salt mixture too.

08:52.698 --> 08:54.200
I was really craving this today.

08:54.283 --> 08:56.744
I wanted to have it
with warm, cooked rice.

09:26.857 --> 09:28.526
DOONA

09:29.318 --> 09:32.738
Sorry, the number you're
trying to reach is currently unavailable.

09:32.822 --> 09:35.616
Please leave a message after the tone.

09:45.626 --> 09:49.255
Didn't we agree
you wouldn't keep a personal cell phone?

09:50.047 --> 09:53.175
Sometimes I just wanna hear your voice,
you know?

09:57.179 --> 09:58.848
Don't cause any trouble.

10:07.940 --> 10:09.734
Aw, you're so cute.

10:11.319 --> 10:12.445
You like me, don't you?

10:13.988 --> 10:15.531
Just be careful with people.

10:15.615 --> 10:17.575
You're better off
staying out of their way.

10:17.658 --> 10:19.410
Lots of bad people out there.

10:20.453 --> 10:21.621
Hmm?

10:21.704 --> 10:23.164
Ah!

10:23.247 --> 10:27.585
Ah. Wow, you're a genius.
You understood me right away.

10:27.668 --> 10:28.836
I'm sorry I scared you.

10:29.462 --> 10:31.255
I'm sorry.

10:32.798 --> 10:35.009
- Are you hurt?
- Hmm?

10:41.557 --> 10:44.352
- You're bleeding.
- It doesn't hurt at all. I'm all right.

10:47.480 --> 10:48.606
Where were you?

10:49.273 --> 10:50.566
I called you earlier.

10:50.650 --> 10:51.567
At my new job.

10:51.651 --> 10:52.485
So you were tutoring?

10:52.568 --> 10:55.613
No, at a café.
I haven't gotten a tutoring job yet.

11:00.242 --> 11:02.703
Do you know the thing
that I really hate the most? Take a guess.

11:03.704 --> 11:06.374
- Uh, horrible singing?
- Ding!

11:07.792 --> 11:09.335
Ignoring my phone calls.

11:12.546 --> 11:13.881
So how can I say it?

11:15.174 --> 11:16.967
It makes me feel abandoned.

11:18.928 --> 11:22.306
- It really sucks.
- Oh, uh, I'm sorry. I didn't mean to.

11:26.727 --> 11:28.813
I wasn't talking about you, actually.

11:30.106 --> 11:31.315
You should rest.

11:33.192 --> 11:34.276
Um, your phone call…

11:34.360 --> 11:37.947
So, uh, why exactly did you call?
Was there something wrong earlier?

11:40.366 --> 11:42.326
Well, I was just hoping
to hear your voice.

11:43.411 --> 11:46.163
- So next time, you should answer my call.
- Hmm.

12:32.501 --> 12:36.046
Hello, and welcome to the 44th
Civil Engineering Student Association.

12:36.130 --> 12:38.507
To kick off the new semester,
the Civil Engineering…

12:38.591 --> 12:41.010
Due to a study group
meeting, I will not be…

12:41.093 --> 12:43.804
20,000 won to attend,
50,000 won to decline.

12:47.349 --> 12:48.559
I will attend.

12:56.776 --> 12:58.110
START-OF-TERM PARTY!

12:59.403 --> 13:00.905
- What's our school?
- Minsong!

13:00.988 --> 13:02.490
- Our department?
- Engineering!

13:02.573 --> 13:03.616
What's our class?

13:03.699 --> 13:04.575
- Civil!
- We are civil!

13:04.658 --> 13:06.660
- Hey! Hey! Hey!
- Civil! Engineering! Civil!

13:06.744 --> 13:07.661
- Let me hear it!
- Hey!

13:07.745 --> 13:09.622
We are number one!

13:25.930 --> 13:28.307
This quarter's results overseas

13:28.390 --> 13:31.894
depend entirely on
the 2022 KCON JAPAN performance.

13:31.977 --> 13:35.189
The single showcase after KCON JAPAN
will be our largest showcase ever.

13:35.272 --> 13:38.567
We plan to expand the media showcase
to the scale of a full concert.

13:38.651 --> 13:41.946
- Of the international artists…
- Doona. Lee Doona.

14:07.304 --> 14:09.890
Hey, take some of this
chaser with your shot, okay?

14:10.933 --> 14:12.393
What's with your expression?

14:13.185 --> 14:14.144
Hey!

14:14.228 --> 14:15.646
LEE DOONA

14:19.316 --> 14:20.818
That's not good enough! Let go!

14:21.318 --> 14:24.196
Hey, if you're sorry, then drink this.
Yeah? You were wrong? You're sorry?

14:24.280 --> 14:26.073
All right. Hey, sit down.

14:26.991 --> 14:27.825
Um, hello?

14:28.325 --> 14:29.785
Hell-low or hell-high?

14:30.494 --> 14:32.246
Wow. That was a bad dad joke!

14:34.164 --> 14:36.500
Where are you? Right now I'm in the area.

14:37.084 --> 14:38.794
Hey there, how are you?

14:40.087 --> 14:42.882
You're the pretty chick I saw
at school the other day, right?

14:42.965 --> 14:44.592
- Come on. Give it back.
- Stop it.

14:46.343 --> 14:48.095
Come on. Stop ignoring me
and say something.

14:48.178 --> 14:50.472
- Please give it back.
- Hello? Anybody there?

14:50.556 --> 14:52.683
Hey, cut it out
and give me back my phone!

14:54.727 --> 14:58.105
- What the hell are you looking at, huh?
- Hey, you!

15:08.908 --> 15:10.242
Did he hit you?

15:10.326 --> 15:11.243
Not yet.

15:13.829 --> 15:15.956
How dare you put your hands on my Won-jun?

15:16.540 --> 15:17.958
So what year are you?

15:18.751 --> 15:20.377
Get your dirty hands off me, kid.

15:20.461 --> 15:22.963
You think 'cause you're pretty
you can do what the fuck you want?

15:23.047 --> 15:24.632
You're starting to piss me off.

15:24.715 --> 15:27.760
Is that right, you total dipshit?
So what are you gonna do about it, huh?

15:27.843 --> 15:30.095
You should worry more
about what I'm gonna do to you.

15:30.179 --> 15:31.889
- Hey, hey, wait.
- Go for it.

15:32.890 --> 15:35.100
Do it, then.

15:35.184 --> 15:37.311
Huh? Huh? Go for it, chick.

15:37.394 --> 15:38.520
Go right on ahead.

15:40.064 --> 15:41.482
Don't cause any more trouble.

15:42.858 --> 15:45.444
I thought you were pissed,
so just hit me already, huh?

15:46.028 --> 15:47.988
If you can't do it,
stop waving that thing around.

15:48.072 --> 15:49.782
- You think that I can't?
- Just do it!

16:11.011 --> 16:13.639
PHARMACY

16:21.230 --> 16:22.064
Ah.

16:25.442 --> 16:26.276
Ah!

16:26.360 --> 16:28.237
Ah.

16:41.333 --> 16:42.584
I don't need to drink that.

16:42.668 --> 16:44.920
I should drink it.
I'm the one who really needs it.

16:52.344 --> 16:53.470
Hmm. Take it.

16:55.055 --> 16:57.641
You can't go around hitting people
over the head with glass bottles.

16:57.725 --> 16:59.893
You'll get arrested immediately.
All right?

16:59.977 --> 17:01.437
He said to do it, didn't he?

17:13.991 --> 17:15.993
Look, I don't know
what your life story might be,

17:16.577 --> 17:19.246
um, but if you need to go
to anger management, uh…

17:20.247 --> 17:22.958
There are resources available for you
if you need treatment.

17:25.711 --> 17:27.838
Why? Do you think I've been through a lot?

17:27.921 --> 17:29.882
- Uh… uh, well…
- Uh-huh?

17:29.965 --> 17:32.051
Normally girls don't walk around the city

17:32.134 --> 17:34.261
with glass bottles
to smash people's heads in.

17:35.179 --> 17:37.014
I wanted to have a drink with you.

17:38.515 --> 17:40.267
I bought it from the beverage store.

17:45.230 --> 17:46.732
Let's grab a drink, Doona.

17:47.483 --> 17:48.567
What's stopping us?

17:57.242 --> 17:58.368
Huh?

17:59.244 --> 18:01.914
Oh, yay!

18:01.997 --> 18:04.792
- Ah, how about fried chicken?
- Okay, fried chicken for you.

18:04.875 --> 18:08.253
This is gonna be so fun.

18:08.337 --> 18:10.506
Fried chicken and beer sounds delicious.

18:10.589 --> 18:13.133
- Wait, how many are we?
- I'm literally starving now.

18:13.217 --> 18:14.051
I can't wait.

18:14.134 --> 18:15.677
I wasn't hungry before.

18:15.761 --> 18:17.846
- Wait here. I'm just gonna go say hi.
- Oh, sure.

18:18.430 --> 18:20.349
Won-jun!

18:21.225 --> 18:23.602
- Were you here for the party?
- Uh-huh. You too?

18:23.685 --> 18:24.853
Mm-hmm.

18:25.604 --> 18:27.606
- Oh, you're with someone.
- Uh, yeah.

18:27.689 --> 18:30.484
We, uh… we live in the same co-ed house.

18:30.567 --> 18:31.652
- She, uh--
- Oh!

18:32.194 --> 18:34.363
Lee Doona?! Is that you?

18:34.446 --> 18:36.657
Hey, Kook Su-jin is a superfan, isn't he?

18:37.533 --> 18:38.659
I'm a fan too.

18:41.370 --> 18:43.288
Let's get going. I'm pretty tired.

18:43.372 --> 18:48.252
Oh! Um, I'm sorry,
but by any chance, do you drink at all?

18:48.335 --> 18:50.212
- You can join us.
- How about another time?

18:50.295 --> 18:53.215
And why would I let
a complete stranger drink with me, again?

18:53.757 --> 18:55.843
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

19:00.347 --> 19:01.640
I'm…

19:02.432 --> 19:03.517
Well, I'm…

19:04.434 --> 19:05.602
I'm honestly

19:07.104 --> 19:08.355
just a shy girl.

19:08.438 --> 19:10.774
- Really shy, actually.
- Hmm.

19:14.570 --> 19:16.405
You're so lucky though, you know that?

19:16.488 --> 19:18.740
I'm serious! You're lucky!

19:20.033 --> 19:20.868
That's right!

19:22.077 --> 19:23.704
And, yeah, like, um…

19:23.787 --> 19:27.332
Well, I… I'm the kind of girl
everyone likes, huh?

19:30.752 --> 19:32.337
Hey, I bet he does too!

19:33.297 --> 19:34.423
Hey, Won-jun.

19:35.299 --> 19:37.009
Uh, you still do, right?

19:37.092 --> 19:40.721
- Um… well, um…
- Who cares if he does or doesn't?

19:40.804 --> 19:42.181
It's not really important.

19:43.265 --> 19:46.518
Hey, Jin-ju.
We should just get married, right?

19:46.602 --> 19:49.021
Okay, Doona, yeah,
I do wanna marry you.

19:49.104 --> 19:51.773
- Yeah, let's get married!
- Let's get married!

19:53.650 --> 19:56.945
Hey, Jin-ju, I think you might
have already missed the subway train.

19:57.029 --> 19:58.363
No, we're tying the knot!

19:58.447 --> 20:01.366
Yeah, quiet, we have to tie the knot!

20:03.952 --> 20:05.954
I think
you missed the last train.

20:06.455 --> 20:07.372
Hmm.

20:08.040 --> 20:09.124
Hey.

20:10.292 --> 20:13.462
Jin-ju, crash at my house tonight, huh?

20:13.545 --> 20:16.215
Actually, you should just live here.

20:17.216 --> 20:18.467
You get all of this.

20:18.967 --> 20:22.012
- I will give you everything--
- I really needed a place to stay, Doona!

20:22.596 --> 20:24.223
Thank you!

20:24.306 --> 20:26.225
Jin-ju, you're crazy for real.

20:26.308 --> 20:27.643
Hey.

20:28.769 --> 20:30.729
Wait, are you crazy?

20:31.897 --> 20:33.857
Yeah, you must be crazy!

20:35.108 --> 20:36.485
Hey, wake up, Jin-ju.

20:36.568 --> 20:38.946
Are you asleep now?

20:39.571 --> 20:40.405
DAD

20:40.489 --> 20:42.074
Hey, why are you sleeping?

20:42.658 --> 20:44.159
- Oh.
- You're crazy.

20:44.660 --> 20:46.745
Jin-ju, wake up.
Your father's calling you right now.

20:46.828 --> 20:48.747
- Jin-ju?
- What's going on?

20:48.830 --> 20:50.749
Oh, what should we do?
We can't just let it ring.

20:50.832 --> 20:51.959
Well, answer the phone.

20:52.042 --> 20:53.585
It'd be really bad if a man answered.

20:56.797 --> 20:59.299
You're a man, huh?

20:59.383 --> 21:01.843
- Oh, he's a man!
- Ah, what do I do?

21:03.095 --> 21:05.973
Huh? Oh, no, you really shouldn't answer.
Um, yes? Hello?

21:11.103 --> 21:12.854
Oh, yes, hello, Mr. Kim?

21:12.938 --> 21:14.147
Why yes, you're so intuitive.

21:14.231 --> 21:15.941
I'm Lee Se-na,
a friend of your daughter's.

21:16.024 --> 21:17.776
We're in literature together.

21:17.859 --> 21:20.529
The start-of-term party
finished a little late tonight,

21:20.612 --> 21:22.531
so she made the decision to stay here.

21:23.615 --> 21:24.616
Oh, Jin-ju is…

21:24.700 --> 21:28.203
She's, um, just in the shower now.
Should I have her call you?

21:29.496 --> 21:32.332
Oh, yes, everything's fine.
Don't worry about her.

21:32.416 --> 21:35.961
Oh, yes, of course. Both my parents
are here in the house. Yes, sir.

21:36.837 --> 21:39.047
I sure will. You have a great night, sir.

21:43.135 --> 21:45.762
Wow, you were so perfect,
like a total natural.

21:45.846 --> 21:47.514
- That was awesome to see.
- Cool.

21:47.597 --> 21:50.767
You should've been
an actor instead, not a pop star.

22:00.027 --> 22:01.737
I'm going for a cigarette now.

22:02.738 --> 22:04.239
You should go home, all right?

22:22.299 --> 22:23.425
Go home, I said.

22:23.508 --> 22:26.595
Uh, Yun-taek told me
not to come home before 2:00.

22:27.429 --> 22:28.472
So I will in a little.

22:33.185 --> 22:34.061
Oh.

22:42.944 --> 22:43.862
Hmm.

22:53.372 --> 22:55.791
What's with your hand?
It's looking pretty rough now.

22:56.291 --> 22:57.334
What?

22:58.085 --> 23:01.630
Ah. It's weird, but I seem
to get injured every time I'm around you.

23:02.964 --> 23:04.633
Maybe we're not meant to hang out.

23:07.094 --> 23:08.595
She's pretty, and you know it.

23:09.513 --> 23:10.555
Jin-ju.

23:11.848 --> 23:13.975
Hmm. She really is.

23:18.313 --> 23:20.273
I'm jealous of that.

23:23.068 --> 23:25.946
Wait. Her being pretty
makes you feel jealous?

23:28.281 --> 23:30.158
No, I'm jealous of you.

23:33.078 --> 23:35.539
You have
this really great relationship with her,

23:36.540 --> 23:38.375
'cause you've known her so long.

23:38.959 --> 23:40.168
That's why I'm jealous of you.

23:46.842 --> 23:48.343
It's so not fair, you know.

23:50.971 --> 23:53.473
I have yet to know
a true friend like that.

23:54.975 --> 23:56.810
Oh! Hey, Doona, be careful.

23:56.893 --> 23:58.895
You've had a lot to drink, remember? Ah.

23:59.896 --> 24:02.774
I sometimes wonder
how I ended up like this in life.

24:07.028 --> 24:08.363
Oh!

24:47.986 --> 24:49.905
You're adorable, you know that?

24:50.697 --> 24:52.365
I almost messed up and did it.

24:52.991 --> 24:54.117
Almost did what?

24:54.201 --> 24:57.245
So if you can manage it,
next time you should turn away.

25:00.040 --> 25:00.916
Hmm.

25:04.836 --> 25:05.795
Mm-mm.

25:24.481 --> 25:27.150
Hey, Doona, be careful.
You've had a lot to drink, remember?

25:27.234 --> 25:28.693
Oh!

25:32.572 --> 25:33.406
Ah.

26:08.441 --> 26:10.569
MINSONG NATIONAL UNIVERSITY JOB FAIR

26:19.327 --> 26:20.161
Uh…

26:20.912 --> 26:22.330
I, uh… I promised washed it.

26:22.914 --> 26:25.083
That's strange.
It still has your smell on it.

26:25.166 --> 26:26.960
I guess it's your fabric softener.

26:29.754 --> 26:31.590
So, did you get home all right yesterday?

26:31.673 --> 26:34.134
Doona said she didn't know
when you had left this morning.

26:34.217 --> 26:36.636
- So when did you head out?
- Oh man, that's right.

26:37.137 --> 26:39.764
I forgot to thank Doona
for letting me sleep over last night,

26:41.182 --> 26:43.184
because somebody had me in shock.

26:43.268 --> 26:44.102
Who?

26:44.728 --> 26:47.522
Won-jun, hey, it's me.
You don't need to hide it.

26:48.315 --> 26:49.274
I saw you guys.

26:50.525 --> 26:52.902
You and Doona kissed. I saw it all.

26:52.986 --> 26:55.280
Kiss? Uh, you did?

26:55.363 --> 26:57.032
Uh-huh!

26:57.574 --> 26:59.618
Oh, Se-hun's here. I'm over here!

27:00.452 --> 27:03.038
- I should go. I'll see you at work, okay?
- Oh.

27:03.121 --> 27:04.664
Uh, I didn't kiss her…

27:09.002 --> 27:10.045
But I…

27:17.510 --> 27:18.970
I didn't kiss her.

27:36.363 --> 27:37.947
This is a milk container.

27:40.241 --> 27:41.951
Cosmetics are general waste.

27:43.536 --> 27:47.791
I guess your manager did this for you.
You obviously haven't had to do it before.

27:50.126 --> 27:51.336
You sound irritated.

27:51.419 --> 27:52.837
Is it because you're hangry?

27:54.089 --> 27:56.341
Or is because Jin-ju rejected you?

27:56.424 --> 27:59.427
Huh? What has she got to do
with any of this? Jeez, come on.

28:00.887 --> 28:02.138
And this is plastic.

28:02.764 --> 28:04.307
You got rejected. Bingo.

28:05.767 --> 28:07.560
I wasn't rejected, okay?

28:08.353 --> 28:10.647
She thinks you and I
have something going on right now.

28:10.730 --> 28:12.357
Hmm? She does?

28:12.440 --> 28:13.900
Why?

28:13.983 --> 28:16.945
Because she saw us that night that, um,

28:17.570 --> 28:18.488
on the roof,

28:18.571 --> 28:20.281
well, uh… yeah.

28:21.366 --> 28:22.784
Ah.

28:25.370 --> 28:26.996
You should've set her straight.

28:28.123 --> 28:31.918
Okay, whatever. It's not like
we're together or anything, right?

28:32.001 --> 28:34.295
Trying to explain it
would just make it more awkward.

28:34.379 --> 28:36.131
So what do we do now?

28:36.214 --> 28:38.133
Should we just date for real, then?

28:40.176 --> 28:43.096
Just so you know, it's very clear to me
now why you don't have friends.

28:51.896 --> 28:52.981
And what makes you say that?

28:53.064 --> 28:57.569
Well, you have no filter when you speak.
You say whatever you're thinking.

28:57.652 --> 28:59.529
There aren't many people like that.

28:59.612 --> 29:02.866
From what I'm seeing, you don't care
what anyone thinks about you.

29:02.949 --> 29:04.743
And you don't feel the need to hold back.

29:05.535 --> 29:06.786
In some ways, I envy you.

29:08.288 --> 29:09.456
Huh? What the heck?

29:10.039 --> 29:11.541
This is also general waste.

29:15.170 --> 29:16.004
Uh-huh.

29:16.755 --> 29:17.630
Yeah.

29:18.757 --> 29:22.302
I do whatever the fuck I want
regardless of what anyone says. So what?

29:22.886 --> 29:23.803
Is that bad? Huh?

29:23.887 --> 29:25.138
Uh… uh…

29:25.221 --> 29:26.097
Ah, I get it now.

29:26.181 --> 29:28.433
I'm alone because of my attitude,
is that it?

29:28.516 --> 29:29.768
It's all on Doona!

29:29.851 --> 29:32.353
I can't possibly fix my career now.
So what? So what?

29:32.437 --> 29:34.981
I should just stick to selling
weight-loss pills on social media?

29:35.064 --> 29:37.442
- Is that what you think, huh?
- Doona, I never said that.

29:37.525 --> 29:40.653
I'm gonna sort the recycling
however the fuck I want, okay?

29:40.737 --> 29:43.281
Don't tell me
where the fuck to put stuff, you hear?

30:07.931 --> 30:09.891
You couldn't just keep it together.

30:24.322 --> 30:27.283
Has it occurred to you
that you brought this upon yourself?

31:01.192 --> 31:02.151
Hey, Kooksu.

31:02.235 --> 31:04.195
You know that girl Doona you love
from Dream Sweet

31:04.279 --> 31:05.738
or whatever they're called?

31:06.239 --> 31:08.825
Yes! The goddess Doona!
Yeah, why?

31:08.908 --> 31:10.535
Is she
going through a hard time?

31:10.618 --> 31:13.413
I hear a lot of celebrities deal with
mental illness and stuff like that.

31:13.496 --> 31:15.456
Maybe she struggled with cyberbullying?

31:15.540 --> 31:16.833
Oh, no way, dude!

31:16.916 --> 31:18.960
Doona just does
whatever the hell she wants to,

31:19.043 --> 31:20.044
and that's how she is.

31:20.128 --> 31:23.172
Yeah, she just left the band to focus on
her studies for now, so I hear.

31:23.256 --> 31:25.258
Please only pay attention to facts
from now on.

31:25.341 --> 31:27.760
- But is that a fact?
- Dude, trust me.

31:27.844 --> 31:30.430
But, hey, why you asking about my girl?

31:31.014 --> 31:33.016
- But it's not a fact?
- Wait, are you a fan?

31:33.099 --> 31:34.559
Oh, don't be ridiculous.

31:34.642 --> 31:36.394
I just thought about her randomly.

31:36.895 --> 31:39.939
Yeah. I, too,
have thought about her a whole lot.

31:40.023 --> 31:41.608
In fact, I think about her all the time.

31:41.691 --> 31:42.901
Yeah, how much is that?

31:42.984 --> 31:43.818
What?

32:45.171 --> 32:47.632
What? Got something to say?

32:47.715 --> 32:50.426
Uh, mm-mm…

32:53.012 --> 32:54.055
Wait, have you eaten yet?

32:58.059 --> 33:00.812
Actually, I cooked way too much food
for dinner just now.

33:01.813 --> 33:03.773
If you haven't eaten,
give me a minute, okay?

33:03.856 --> 33:06.359
- Wait here. I'll bring it down to you.
- Wait, don't.

33:30.425 --> 33:31.968
- Hey.
- Hmm?

33:32.051 --> 33:34.804
Don't you know it's a rule to give notice
before you bring a guest over?

33:34.887 --> 33:37.515
I didn't exactly bring her over just now.

33:38.558 --> 33:41.185
- So, she actually lives right below us.
- Exactly!

33:41.894 --> 33:45.023
Instead, why don't you give notice
about how antisocial you are

33:45.106 --> 33:46.315
so the poor girl can dodge you?

33:49.986 --> 33:52.113
Pay no attention
to this heartless jerk, okay?

33:52.196 --> 33:57.160
And, uh, come visit us
anytime you want to, hmm? Okay?

34:12.467 --> 34:14.969
Can I, um…
can I ask you a personal question?

34:15.887 --> 34:18.181
Uh… and don't feel like
you have to answer me.

34:18.765 --> 34:20.641
Mm-hmm. Fire away.

34:21.726 --> 34:22.894
Why did you quit Dream Sweet?

34:27.482 --> 34:30.276
Maybe I haven't accomplished
enough in life to get it, hmm,

34:31.027 --> 34:33.821
but I can't imagine someone
who's worked as hard as you

34:34.322 --> 34:35.740
just giving up on it.

34:37.909 --> 34:40.745
Sorry. You must get
these kinds of questions all the time.

34:42.038 --> 34:44.874
Actually, you're the first one to ask me.

34:45.541 --> 34:46.626
Oh, really?

34:47.210 --> 34:50.129
In my experience, I find that people
will believe what they want to.

34:50.213 --> 34:52.298
They don't care to know the actual truth.

34:57.720 --> 34:59.055
But if I had to be honest…

35:01.057 --> 35:02.850
there wasn't a reason why I quit.

35:05.019 --> 35:06.604
I just unexpectedly…

35:09.816 --> 35:10.983
couldn't sing at all anymore.

35:12.819 --> 35:13.986
The end, hmm?

35:32.880 --> 35:34.215
Do you have any change?

35:36.676 --> 35:38.177
All right. Good luck.

35:39.887 --> 35:41.430
Here I go…

35:41.514 --> 35:44.142
Ah!

35:45.768 --> 35:48.271
- Oh!
- Oh! Oh!

35:48.771 --> 35:50.398
Ah.

35:55.486 --> 35:57.363
- Ah! Oh.
- Oh. Oh.

35:57.446 --> 35:59.615
- Ah.
- Ah, seriously?! No!

35:59.699 --> 36:01.868
Oh! Oh!

36:07.123 --> 36:08.624
- Really? All of this?
- Mm-hmm.

36:12.879 --> 36:13.921
Hurry up. I need it!

36:14.630 --> 36:15.548
Here you go.

36:21.846 --> 36:23.514
Oh! Oh!

36:25.892 --> 36:28.019
Oh!

36:33.191 --> 36:34.650
You should've kept it together.

36:35.735 --> 36:38.279
Now go back out there and sing.
We'll talk after.

36:42.241 --> 36:44.577
Dream Sweet,
you're on in three minutes!

36:44.660 --> 36:45.828
We're starting now!

36:45.912 --> 36:47.830
I don't think I can sing tonight.

36:47.914 --> 36:49.415
What do you mean you can't sing?

36:49.916 --> 36:51.542
My anxiety is through the roof.

36:53.377 --> 36:55.504
You're going on stage… no matter what.

36:56.214 --> 36:58.549
Enough of your nonsense.
Now, get out there.

37:04.597 --> 37:06.140
Ten seconds!

37:10.394 --> 37:11.395
Five seconds!

37:11.479 --> 37:13.189
Four. Three.

37:13.272 --> 37:14.482
Two.

38:21.882 --> 38:24.427
Hey, Lee Doona!
You really let yourself go!

38:27.263 --> 38:29.140
Can you bite on this
just once for me?

38:38.190 --> 38:39.525
You have to make a point?

38:39.608 --> 38:41.485
Ugh! Seriously?!

38:43.029 --> 38:45.281
You wanna be a diva?
Leave it for your solo career.

38:52.788 --> 38:54.290
A CERTAIN BIG STAR IS SUPER RUDE

38:54.373 --> 38:55.666
This is plagiarism!

38:55.750 --> 38:57.877
They're obviously identical
down to the composition!

38:57.960 --> 39:00.588
Hey, you!
You're gonna lose everything and end up

39:00.671 --> 39:03.257
selling weight loss pills on social media!

39:08.846 --> 39:10.973
Did something happen?

39:11.057 --> 39:13.309
What's wrong with her?
What's happening on stage?

39:21.984 --> 39:23.110
Doona.

39:23.194 --> 39:24.362
Lee Doona!

39:25.237 --> 39:26.405
Wake up.

39:27.531 --> 39:28.491
Lee Doona!

39:36.791 --> 39:39.460
Whoo! I did it! Oh!

39:47.510 --> 39:48.928
- Let's go!
- Okay.

39:59.855 --> 40:03.150
- Today was my birthday, you know.
- Ah, seriously?

40:03.651 --> 40:06.529
And I happened to make
birthday seaweed soup? Wow.

40:07.988 --> 40:09.615
You should eat better, you know?

40:09.698 --> 40:11.325
Food makes everything better
in my opinion.

40:11.409 --> 40:13.702
Although I don't have
much going on in my life,

40:14.286 --> 40:18.124
I find that eating well can really,
uh, um, boost my morale these days.

40:22.628 --> 40:23.587
So what's the deal?

40:24.255 --> 40:26.173
What's the story between Jin-ju and you?

40:28.676 --> 40:32.471
Well, I think that's
how things go with high-school crushes.

40:33.472 --> 40:36.225
Like a fool, you begin to read
way too much into every little detail.

40:36.851 --> 40:39.812
First it's despair. Then you're floating
in the clouds sometimes no reason.

40:39.895 --> 40:41.689
Then you overdo it,

40:42.857 --> 40:44.817
and things end up falling apart, right?

40:47.945 --> 40:51.115
- You're sure she doesn't have feelings?
- Yes, I'm sure, Doona.

40:51.198 --> 40:52.366
I think you're wrong.

40:52.450 --> 40:53.451
How do you know?

40:53.534 --> 40:56.120
- Never mind that. You could court her.
- And how would I do that?

40:56.912 --> 40:58.581
You make her heart race.

40:59.790 --> 41:01.917
Girls like Jin-ju wanna feel like that.

41:02.501 --> 41:04.962
You should put her against the wall.

41:06.464 --> 41:09.425
Just think about it.
Push her up against any wall.

41:09.508 --> 41:12.595
Then look at her
and don't even say a single word to her

41:12.678 --> 41:13.846
for ten seconds.

41:14.346 --> 41:16.682
No, you won't need ten. Five is plenty.

41:17.933 --> 41:19.143
And then…

41:20.644 --> 41:22.521
What? And then what?

41:26.859 --> 41:28.194
You come up with the next part.

41:29.278 --> 41:31.071
I can't do everything for you, huh?

41:32.156 --> 41:33.699
Won-Jun, you're so demanding.

41:37.828 --> 41:39.622
You could always practice with me.

41:40.247 --> 41:41.540
And I'll tell you

41:41.624 --> 41:43.501
if my heart starts racing.

41:45.669 --> 41:46.670
Uh…

42:02.937 --> 42:04.438
Happy birthday to you.

42:08.442 --> 42:11.111
See?
I'm not good at that this at all, right?

42:13.822 --> 42:16.742
Let's get going.
It's late, and your birthday is over, hmm?

43:11.338 --> 43:14.300
Uh, it's me. Were you already sleeping?

43:16.218 --> 43:17.052
No.

43:19.388 --> 43:21.223
Why? You have something to say?

43:21.849 --> 43:24.101
Um, yeah, well, um, just so you know,

43:24.184 --> 43:26.395
there's nothing between Doona and I, okay?

43:26.478 --> 43:28.480
I think you had the wrong idea earlier,

43:28.564 --> 43:31.525
um, and well, I hope
that makes things more clear.

43:34.320 --> 43:35.195
Oh yeah?

43:37.156 --> 43:37.990
All right.

43:42.369 --> 43:43.329
I'm glad.

43:50.711 --> 43:52.838
Happy birthday. I'll be in touch.
